.TH MEMSPYCTL 1 "October 2026" "MemSpy 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memspyctl \- inspect and administer the local MemSpy detector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memspyctl
.RI [ --json ]
.IR command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memspyctl
is a non-interactive client for the local MemSpy Unix socket at
.IR /run/memspy/memspy.sock .
The caller must be a trusted member of the
.B memspy-ui
group. No network connection is created.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show detector, storage, event-loss, and response health.
.TP
.B alerts [--limit 1..200] [--minimum medium|high]
List newest alerts.
.TP
.B show ALERT_ID
Show all evidence for one alert.
.TP
.B export ALERT_ID
Write one canonical alert JSON document to standard output.
.TP
.B response on|off
Request a PolicyKit-authorized response-mode change.
.TP
.B version
Print the client version.
.SH OUTPUT
Human-readable output is the default. With
.B --json
before the command or after status, alerts, show, or response, standard output contains only one JSON document; diagnostics are written to standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 invalid usage; 3 detector or API unavailable; 4 authorization failure; 5 alert not found.
.SH SECURITY
Alert data can contain command lines and process paths for all local users. Add only trusted administrators to
.BR memspy-ui .
PolicyKit handles administrator credentials; MemSpy never reads a password.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memspyd (8),
.BR memspy-ui (1)
